	<key>readme</key>
	<string>PREREQ: run ./setup.sh in the prototype directory, put your Anthropic key in ~/.aardvark-proto-key (chmod 600), then ./regen.sh and import this file.

Keyword: `avemoji`. Type a folder title (or `title | description`). The offline emoji candidates appear at once; "Asking Claude…" sits at the top with a live wait counter; when the API answers, its pick jumps to the top tagged with how long it took. Pick any row to fire a notification showing the chosen emoji and its source.

Re-feel it against several titles. `rm -rf` the PROTO_CACHE dir (printed by setup.sh) to force fresh calls - a second entry of the same title is served from cache instantly, which is itself a finding.

What to watch: does the wait feel blocking or does showing offline-first hide it? Is the rerun swap jarring? On a slow or failed call, does the fallback read as broken?</string>
